Design a decoder for a 4-bit input that translates hexadecimal values (0 through F) into corresponding 7-segment display outputs. The module takes a 4-bit binary input and uses a combinatorial logic to drive a 7-segment display, representing numbers 0-9 and letters A-F on the display. Each hexadecimal digit is mapped to a specific 7-bit pattern that controls which segments of the display are illuminated, with a default state that turns all segments off for invalid inputs.
module top_module(
    input  wire  [3:0] value,
    output reg   [6:0] seg
);

