description:
Implement a pulse-width modulation (PWM) circuit that generates an output signal varying its width based on the provided 16-bit input, which determines the duty cycle. The circuit uses a clock input to manage timing and counts up to a defined frequency. The reference signal is derived by shifting the input to match the desired resolution, while the output signal is asserted high when the counter surpasses the reference value, effectively controlling the duty cycle of the PWM signal. The counter resets after reaching a limit calculated from the frequency, allowing for continuous PWM signal generation.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [15:0] in,
  output reg out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [15:0] in,
  output reg out
);parameter resolution = 8;
parameter frequency = 100;

reg [resolution-1:0] duty_cycle;
reg [15:0] reference_signal;
reg [31:0] counter;

assign reference_signal = in >> (16 - resolution);

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (counter >= reference_signal) begin
    out <= 1;
  end else begin
    out <= 0;
  end

  counter <= counter + 1;
  if (counter >= (1 << 16) / frequency) begin
    counter <= 0;
  end

  duty_cycle <= counter >> (16 - resolution);
end

endmodule

