description:
Design a binary to one-hot encoder that converts a 4-bit binary input B into an 8-bit one-hot output O. For each valid binary value (1, 2, 4, or 8 corresponding to the binary representations of 4'b0001, 4'b0010, 4'b0100, and 4'b1000), the output O will have a single bit set to high (1) at the position indicated by the binary input, while all other bits remain low (0). For any other input, the output will be all low (0).
module top_module(
    input [3:0] B,
    output reg [7:0] O
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] B,
    output reg [7:0] O
);always @(*)
begin
    case(B)
        4'b0001: O = 8'b00000001;
        4'b0010: O = 8'b00000010;
        4'b0100: O = 8'b00000100;
        4'b1000: O = 8'b00001000;
        default: O = 8'b00000000;
    endcase
end

endmodule

