description:
Design a circuit that decodes ALU operations based on a two-bit ALU operation code (ALUOP) and a six-bit function code (funct). This module outputs a three-bit ALU control signal (ALUControl) that determines the specific operation to perform within the Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU). It utilizes a combinational logic approach to select the appropriate ALUControl based on predefined ALUOP values, with specific provisions for the funct input to handle certain operations, returning the corresponding control signals for operations like addition and defaulting to a no-operation state for unrecognized inputs.
module top_module(
    ALUOP, funct, ALUControl
);

code:
module top_module(
    ALUOP, funct, ALUControl
);input [1:0] ALUOP;
input [5:0] funct;
output reg [2:0] ALUControl;

always@(*) begin
  case(ALUOP)
    0: ALUControl <= 1;
    1: ALUControl <= 7;
    2: 
    begin 
        case (funct)
            6'h20: ALUControl <= 1;
            default: ALUControl <= 0;
        endcase
    end
    default: ALUControl <= 0;
  endcase
end

endmodule

