description:
Design a 4-to-2 priority encoder that takes a 4-bit binary input and outputs a 2-bit position indicating the highest priority active input. The module assigns the output based on the input conditions, prioritizing the most significant bit (MSB) when multiple inputs are active, ensuring that the output reflects the position of the highest active bit. If no inputs are active, it defaults to outputting the lowest position.
module top_module(
  input [3:0] in,
  output reg [1:0] pos
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [3:0] in,
  output reg [1:0] pos
);always @(*) begin
    case(in)
      4'b0001: pos = 2'b00;
      4'b0010: pos = 2'b01;
      4'b0100: pos = 2'b10;
      4'b1000: pos = 2'b11;
      4'b0011: pos = 2'b01;
      4'b0101: pos = 2'b10;
      4'b0110: pos = 2'b10;
      4'b1001: pos = 2'b11;
      4'b1010: pos = 2'b11;
      4'b1100: pos = 2'b11;
      default: pos = 2'b00;
    endcase
  end

endmodule

